From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: glacier <hyouga.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 03:23:29 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Skip the neighbour position when a block has no physics
 handler

World.applyPhysics probed six neighbours through blockposition.west(),
east(), and so on, allocating a BlockPosition for each one on every block
change - redstone, fluid flow, placing and breaking.

A shared mutable position is not safe here: notifyBlockOfStateChange
hands the position to doPhysics, and a block may schedule an update,
which stores the reference in NextTickListEntry. Reusing one instance
would corrupt those entries later.

Instead the probes are now driven by coordinate. Block.doPhysics is empty
by default, so notifyBlockOfStateChange(x, y, z, block) reads the
neighbour's state by coordinate and returns immediately unless the block
declares a physics handler or a plugin is listening for BlockPhysicsEvent
- no position is built at all for the usual stone, dirt and air
neighbours. The 46 blocks that implement doPhysics override
hasPhysicsHandler(), which subclasses inherit.

Behaviour is unchanged: getType(x, y, z) and getType(BlockPosition) both
resolve to getType(x, y, z, true), and the event still fires for every
neighbour whenever a listener is registered.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/Block.java b/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/Block.java
index 0d88d40e19fdbbe2bef7b7eb13973ddb603d1784..2ebd972a9ec09d03981fce18921af4e20f47ed94 100644
--- a/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/Block.java
+++ b/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/Block.java
@@ -355,6 +355,14 @@ public class Block {
 
     public void doPhysics(World world, BlockPosition blockposition, IBlockData iblockdata, Block block) {}
 
+    // Athena - true when this block actually reacts to a neighbour change. The default doPhysics is
+    // empty, so World.notifyBlockOfStateChange can skip building a BlockPosition entirely for the
+    // overwhelmingly common case of stone/dirt/air neighbours. Declaring doPhysics implies this, and
+    // subclasses inherit the override.
+    public boolean hasPhysicsHandler() {
+        return false;
+    }
+
     public int tickRate(World world) {
         return 10;
     }
